e."}}},{"verse_id":60389,"page_no":1430,"line_no":14,"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਰੀਰਾਗ ਸਿਉ ਪਾਂਚਉ ਥਾਪੀ ॥੧॥","translit_en":"sireeraag siau paa(n)chau thaapee ||1||","translation":{"en":{"bdb":"These are the five wives of Siree Raag. ||1||"}}},{"verse_id":60390,"page_no":1430,"line_no":14,"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਲੂ ਸਾਰਗ ਸਾਗਰਾ ਅਉਰ ਗੋਂਡ ਗੰਭੀਰ ॥","translit_en":"saaloo saarag saagaraa aaur go(n)dd ga(n)bheer ||","translation":{"en":{"bdb":"Saaloo, Saarang, Saagaraa, Gond and Gambheer"}}},{"verse_id":60391,"page_no":1430,"line_no":15,"gurmukhi":"ਅਸਟ ਪੁਤ੍ਰ ਸ੍ਰੀਰਾਗ ਕੇ ਗੁੰਡ ਕੁੰਭ ਹਮੀਰ ॥੧॥","translit_en":"asaT putr sreeraag ke gu(n)dd ku(n)bh hameer ||1||","translation":{"en":{"bdb":"- the eight sons of Siree Raag include Gund, Kumb and Hameer. ||1||"}}},{"verse_id":60392,"page_no":1430,"line_no":15,"gurmukhi":"ਖਸਟਮ ਮੇਘ ਰਾਗ ਵੈ ਗਾਵਹਿ ॥","translit_en":"khasaTam megh raag vai gaaveh ||","translation":{"en":{"bdb":"In the sixth place, Maygh Raag is sung,"}}},{"verse_id":60393,"page_no":1430,"line_no":16,"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਂਚਉ ਸੰਗਿ ਬਰੰਗਨ ਲਾਵਹਿ ॥","translit_en":"paa(n)chau sa(n)g bara(n)gan laaveh ||","translation":{"en":{"bdb":"with its five wives in accompaniment:"}}},{"verse_id":60394,"page_no":1430,"line_no":16,"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਿ ਗੋਂਡ ਮਲਾਰੀ ਧੁਨੀ ॥","translit_en":"soraTh go(n)dd malaaree dhunee ||","translation":{"en":{"bdb":"Sorat'h, Gond, and the melody of Malaaree;"}}},{"verse_id":60395,"page_no":1430,"line_no":16,"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਨਿ ਗਾਵਹਿ ਆਸਾ ਗੁਨ ਗੁਨੀ ॥","translit_en":"pun gaaveh aasaa gun gunee ||","translation":{"en":{"bdb":"then the harmonies of Aasaa are sung."}}},{"verse_id":60396,"page_no":1430,"line_no":17,"gurmukhi":"ਊਚੈ ਸੁਰਿ ਸੂਹਉ ਪੁਨਿ ਕੀਨੀ ॥","translit_en":"uoochai sur soohau pun keenee ||","translation":{"en":{"bdb":"And finally comes the high tone Soohau."}}},{"verse_id":60397,"page_no":1430,"line_no":17,"gurmukhi":"ਮੇਘ ਰਾਗ ਸਿਉ ਪਾਂਚਉ ਚੀਨੀ ॥੧॥","translit_en":"megh raag siau paa(n)chau cheenee ||1||","translation":{"en":{"bdb":"These are the five with Maygh Raag. ||1||"}}},{"verse_id":60398,"page_no":